        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Vinegar kills weeds the way a lawn mower does: it removes what is above ground, fast and satisfyingly, and leaves the roots to try again. On young annual weeds in sun, a registered 20% product is a genuinely good tool. On perennials, it is a holding action you will repeat all season.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Use it where a burn-down is enough, protect your eyes and skin like you would with any other chemical, leave the salt out, and for the patches that keep coming back, reach for something that gets to the roots or seal the gap they are growing in.
          </p>
